# Tokens

Tokens are used for authenticating an Adafruit IO user. See the _Authentication_ page for more information about this.

<aside class="warning">
Tokens cannot be created, updated, or deleted individually. <code>POST /tokens</code> <strong>regenerates your Adafruit IO key</strong>: it creates a new key and immediately deactivates all of your previous keys, and any existing connections using the old keys are disconnected. Every device, script, or integration using the old key will stop working until you give it the new key.
</aside>

Only one key is active at a time. <code>DELETE</code>, <code>PUT</code>, and <code>PATCH</code> requests to the tokens endpoints always return <code>400 Bad Request</code>.

## Get All Tokens

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-get">GET</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/tokens</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/tokens
```

```python
```

```cpp
```

```ruby
```

> Response Sample:

```json
[
  {
    "id": 123,
    "key": "aio_xxxx00xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
    "name": null,
    "status": "active",
    "master": true,
    "readable": true,
    "createable": true,
    "updateable": true,
    "deleteable": true,
    "expiration": null,
    "feed_id": null,
    "qr_code": "data:image/png;base64,...",
    "user_id": 456,
    "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
  }
]
```

An array of your active tokens. Inactive (replaced) keys are not returned.




### Path Parameters


Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string



## Regenerate Token

> HTTP Request
> <div class="http"><span class="method-post">POST</span><code class="path">/api/v2/{username}/tokens</code></div>

```shell
$ curl -X POST -H "X-AIO-Key: {io_key}" https://io.adafruit.com/api/v2/{username}/tokens
```

```python
```

```cpp
```

```ruby
```

> Response Sample:

```json
{
  "id": 123,
  "key": "aio_xxxx00xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx",
  "name": null,
  "status": "active",
  "master": true,
  "readable": true,
  "createable": true,
  "updateable": true,
  "deleteable": true,
  "expiration": null,
  "feed_id": null,
  "qr_code": "data:image/png;base64,...",
  "user_id": 456,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
}
```

The new token, returned with status `201 Created`. **All previous keys are now inactive.**



### Path Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
username | string | true | a valid username string


### Body Parameters

Parameter |   Type  |  Required |       Description
--------- | ------- | --------- | -----------------------
token | object | false | optional settings for the new key: `master`, `expiration`, `feed_id`. Omit the body to create a normal full-access key.



## Returns Token

